# crossfader2 RAM accounting (manual/circuits/experimental/crossfader2.md:
# ram_bytes 56 — crossfader's 40 plus 16 for the curve/loop flags and the
# four knot values + two tangents held while a segment is evaluated).
# Hand-computed Forge accounting on a MASTER (typeOfMaster()==16 always adds
# the X7's 864 bytes, attached or not):
#   x7                          864
#   crossfader2 base             56
#   input1 = I1 (simple input)    8
#   input2 = I2 (simple input)    8
#   fade   = I3 (simple input)    8
#   output = O1 (output)          4
#   constants                    16   (seeded {0.0, 1.0} = 8 -> ALIGN_UP(8,16))
#   --------------------------------
#   total                       964
# The same lines under [crossfader] cost 948 (ram-vs-crossfader.gold): the
# two circuits differ by exactly the 16-byte base delta. Patching `curve = 1`
# or `loop = 1` would add 4 bytes each (the 0/1 simple-input optimization).
experimental
expect_ram 964
patch <<<
[crossfader2]
    input1 = I1
    input2 = I2
    fade   = I3
    output = O1
>>>
@0 set I1 0.2
@0 set I2 0.8
@0 set I3 0.5
@0 expect O1 0.5
